13. The Court shall consist of—

(a) the Chancellor;

(b) the Pro-Chancellors;

(c) the Vice-Chancellor;

(d) the members for the time being of the Council;

(e) the members for the time being of the Senate;

(f) eight persons appointed by|the Yang di-Pertuan Agong;

(g) alee persons one appointed by each Ruler or Governor of
a State;

(h) two persons appointed by the Yang di-Pertuan Negara of
Singapore;

(i) one person appointed by the Sultan of Brunei;

(j) one person appointed by the Governor of North Borneo;

(k) one person appointed by the Governor of Sarawak;

UNIVERSITY OH MALAYA                         299

(I) such representatives of the |Guild of Graduates as may be
prescribed by Statute;

(m) such representatives of the] Federal and State Legislatures
and local authorities as may be prescribed by Statute;

(n) such representatives of organizations engaged in teaching or
research, learned societies, hospitals and educational
institutions as may be prescribed by Statute; and

(0) not more than thirty persdns appointed by the Chancellor
on the recommendation} of the Vice-Chancellor being
persons representative / of professional, commercial,
industrial, cultural and other organizations in Malaya.

14. The Court shall, subject to the| provisions of this Constitution,
have power—
(a) to receive an annual report on the University from the
Vice-Chancellor;
(b) to receive such special reports as the Council may decide to
submit to the Court;
(c) to receive the audited anntial accounts of the University;
(d) to pass such resolutions relating to any reports or accounts
submitted to the Court as the Court may think fit;
(e) to receive copies of all Statutes;
(f) to pass such resolutions relating to any Statute received by
the Court as the Court may think fit;
(g) to exercise such other functions as may be conferred on the
Court by Statute.
